ORDER BY through Map insertion order, which Story 5's CLI parity comparison will rely on), and the compact embed shares the standalone walk. Re-ran verify-all after pass 2's manifest addition since the prior epic-gate run predated it: 300 tests pass. Reconciled the test-count convention against the log's own Cumulative Baselines section (which pins verify-all counts: baseline 290, expected ~300): actual is exactly 300, so this payload's totals now follow the log's convention (totalAfterStory 300, delta +10; default suite 273) and the log's Latest Actual Total was updated from 290 to 300 — this also resolves the log's lesson-5 baseline-definition ambiguity for this story by deferring to the log's stated definition. Handoff obligations checked against the log structure: the Story 3 receipt section (## Story Receipts) and Current Continuation Handles entries are written at the receipt step after the verify follow-up, not by the implementor — called out as the explicit remaining handoff work. Two design-accepted residual risks restated for the verifier rather than silently carried.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts\",\"reason\":\"New: reason-code classification table as data (unclassified ⇒ permanent), report walk over both owners, bucket ready/in-flight/blocked/failed×classify, transient requeue through owners' surfaces with already_queued noop counted in-flight, per-owner/kind receipt assembly. No waiting, no provider calls, no direct work_item/derived_form writes (verified structurally in pass 2).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"sweep surface op real (stub removed); compact gains the default-on sweep step with sweep:false skip, post-validation/pre-write so a sweep failure leaves the prior view intact; standalone and embedded paths share runSweep, making AC-3.7's same-receipt-shape structural.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"reason\":\"CompactReceipt.sweep flipped from SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} | \\\"absent\\\" to SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} — Story 2's debt comment closed.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\",\"reason\":\"New: assertSweepReceiptShape — the single structural validator both the Story 3 SDK leg and Story 5's spawned CLI parity leg assert against (TC-3.3's shared-schema mechanism).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"Re-exports assertSweepReceiptShape and the classification table (REASON_CLASS_TABLE/classifyFailureReason) — fixtures are the boundary-exempt bridge for the story-sanctioned exported-for-tests table.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"New: 10 tests covering TC-3.1–3.4, the classification-edge architecture-risk legs (blocked never requeued, structural noop dedupe, unclassified-permanent via the production terminal write path), the table unit legs, and the zero-provider assertion completed across all five thread-view ops.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Sanctioned amendment: sweep is real now, so its not-implemented stub leg moved out; materialize keeps the stub assertion until Story 5.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Sanctioned amendment: receipt assertion flipped from sweep:\\\"absent\\\" to the embedded SweepReceipt, asserting the file's first default compact requeues the fixture's transient failure.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-recorded hashes for the two sanctioned amendments; view-sweep.test.ts recorded (pass 2) so the immutability gate covers the new suite going forward (37 files).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md\",\"reason\":\"Phase updated to implement COMPLETE with recovery detail, SV-03-001/002 closure evidence, gate results, retained verifier handle; pass 3 updated Cumulative Baselines' Latest Actual Total to 300 per the log's verify-all counting convention.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.1: buckets the five seeded states, requeues only the transient failure, returns without waiting, zero provider calls\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.2 (AC-3.4): a second sweep without draining reports the requeued form in-flight and writes no second row\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.3 schema leg (AC-3.5, AC-3.7): the SDK receipt validates against the shared receipt schema\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: zero-provider assertion across all five ops (architecture-risk)\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: blocked forms are reported with their stored reasons and never requeued\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: once-per-invocation dedupe is structural: a turn's two transiently-failed forms share one work row, the second ask noops to in-flight\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: an unclassified reason code lands in permanentFailed with its literal reason and is never requeued\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: the classification table is data: named classes map as designed, everything else is permanent\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: compact with sweep: false records the skip and requeues nothing\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: default compact embeds the sweep receipt; the drained requeue heals into the next compact's view\"],\"modified\":[\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: surface skeleton stub leg (sweep removed from the not-implemented set; materialize-only now)\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: compacts with a built-in profile (sweep:\\\"absent\\\" assertion replaced with embedded-receipt + requeue assertion)\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":300,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":10},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":3,\"findingsFixed\":[\"Pass 3: test-count reporting reconciled to the log's own Cumulative Baselines convention (verify-all counts) — totalAfterStory is 300 against the recorded 290 baseline, exactly the +10 estimate; the log's Latest Actual Total updated 290→300. verify-all re-run after pass 2's manifest change: 300 pass.\",\"Pass 2 (carried): view-sweep.test.ts recorded into the red-manifest so the immutability gate protects the new suite (37 files).\",\"Pass 1 (carried): TC-3.4 heal leg rewritten to drive the drain through a background-SDK compact's requeue poke-on-commit (the production path) instead of a touch-suppressed status call.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"Handoff obligation remaining (next step, not implementor's): the team-impl-log's ## Story Receipts section needs the 03-readiness-sweep receipt entry and Current Continuation Handles needs the verifier-handle update at the receipt step after the verify follow-up.\",\"Design-accepted residual risk (Deferred Items, restated): there is no cross-invocation requeue cap — a failure that persists a transient-class code but never heals re-requeues at every compact, spending one provider attempt cycle each time; receipt visibility is the v1 mitigation.\",\"If an owner requeue fails mid-walk, sweep returns the error and that invocation's receipt is lost; committed requeues are durable and surface as in-flight on the next sweep — partial-failure receipt accounting was not specified.\",\"AC-3.7's CLI execution leg is the story's explicit Scope-out to Story 5's process suite; the shared receipt-schema validator landed here for that leg to assert against.\",\"Untested edge (schema-valid, outside the plan's TC set): sweep on a thread with no derived forms returns an empty-owners receipt.\",\"view-compact.test.ts's record-untouched assertions depend on the file's first default compact performing the fixture's one transient requeue — order coupling documented in the amended test comment.\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Run the story-verify follow-up on the retained verifier handle (codex/019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6) against SV-03-001/SV-03-002 closure, then write the Story 3 receipt into the team-impl-log and commit. CLI parity leg for sweep (TC-3.3 execution half) lands in Story 5's process suite as planned.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"self-review-pass\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/010-self-review-pass-1.json\"},{\"kind\":\"self-review-pass\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/011-self-review-pass-2.json\"},{\"kind\":\"self-review-pass\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/012-self-review-pass-3.json\"},{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/013-self-review-batch.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:19:28.952Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:24:14.928Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
