ero-provider completion), amended the two stale placeholder assertions in view-pull/view-compact under the established sanctioned-amendment pattern (red-manifest re-recorded for those two files), and re-exported the classification table through test/fixtures (the boundary-exempt bridge). One test fix during the run: the heal leg initially drove the drain via a background status call, which is deliberately touch-suppressed (SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001); switched to running the default compact through a background SDK so the embedded requeue's poke-on-commit drives the production repair, which is the design's named path. Both gates green.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts\",\"reason\":\"New (from partial worktree, verified): reason-code classification table as data (unclassified ⇒ permanent), report walk over both owners, bucket ready/in-flight/blocked/failed×classify, transient requeue through owners' surfaces with already_queued noop counted in-flight, per-owner/kind receipt assembly. No waiting, no provider, no direct work_item/derived_form writes.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"From partial worktree, verified: sweep surface op real (stub removed); compact gains the default-on sweep step with sweep:false skip, runs post-validation/pre-write so a sweep failure leaves the prior view intact; receipt embeds the sweep outcome.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"reason\":\"CompactReceipt.sweep flipped from SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} | \\\"absent\\\" to SweepReceipt | {skipped:true} — Story 2's debt comment closed.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\",\"reason\":\"New (from partial worktree, verified): assertSweepReceiptShape — the single structural validator both the Story 3 SDK leg and Story 5's spawned CLI parity leg assert against (TC-3.3's shared-schema mechanism).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"Re-exports assertSweepReceiptShape and the classification table (REASON_CLASS_TABLE/classifyFailureReason) — fixtures are the boundary-exempt bridge for the story-sanctioned exported-for-tests table.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-sweep.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"New: 10 tests covering TC-3.1–3.4, the classification-edge architecture-risk legs (blocked, structural noop dedupe, unclassified-permanent through the production terminal path), the table unit legs, and the zero-provider assertion completed across all five thread-view ops.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Sanctioned amendment: sweep is real now, so its not-implemented stub leg moved out; materialize keeps the stub assertion until Story 5.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Sanctioned amendment: the receipt assertion flipped from sweep:\\\"absent\\\" to the embedded SweepReceipt, asserting the file's first default compact requeues the fixture's transient failure (which keeps the later record-untouched assertions honest).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-recorded hashes for the two sanctioned amendments (record-red-manifest.mjs), keeping the test-immutability gate meaningful.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md\",\"reason\":\"Phase updated to implement COMPLETE with recovery detail, SV-03-001/002 closure evidence, gate results, and the retained verifier handle for the follow-up verify; lessons entry 6 (transient provider failure wedges composed runs) was already recorded by the impl-lead.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.1: buckets the five seeded states, requeues only the transient failure, returns without waiting, zero provider calls\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.2 (AC-3.4): a second sweep without draining reports the requeued form in-flight and writes no second row\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.3 schema leg (AC-3.5, AC-3.7): the SDK receipt validates against the shared receipt schema\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: zero-provider assertion across all five ops (architecture-risk)\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: blocked forms are reported with their stored reasons and never requeued\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: once-per-invocation dedupe is structural: a turn's two transiently-failed forms share one work row, the second ask noops to in-flight\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: an unclassified reason code lands in permanentFailed with its literal reason and is never requeued\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: the classification table is data: named classes map as designed, everything else is permanent\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: compact with sweep: false records the skip and requeues nothing\",\"test/view-sweep.test.ts :: TC-3.4: default compact embeds the sweep receipt; the drained requeue heals into the next compact's view\"],\"modified\":[\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: surface skeleton stub leg (sweep removed from the not-implemented set; materialize-only now)\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: compacts with a built-in profile (sweep:\\\"absent\\\" assertion replaced with embedded-receipt + requeue assertion)\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":273,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":10},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"SV-03-001 (critical): sweep production path was the Story 2 placeholder — closed; internal/sweep.ts + surface + compact embed verified against the owners' report/requeue contracts and Flow 3's bucket rules.\",\"SV-03-002 (major): Story 3 test coverage absent and existing tests asserted placeholder behavior — closed; view-sweep.test.ts added and the two stale assertions amended with the red-manifest re-recorded.\",\"TC-3.4 heal leg initially drove the drain via a background status call, which is touch-suppressed by design (SV-01-PULL-STATUS-001); rewritten to compact through a background SDK so the requeue's poke-on-commit drives the production repair path.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"If an owner requeue fails mid-walk, sweep returns the error and the receipt for already-committed requeues from that invocation is lost (each requeue is its own owner transaction, so they remain durable and the next sweep reports them in-flight). Receipt-level partial-failure accounting was not specified by the story; flagging for verifier awareness.\",\"Default-on sweep means compact in manual mode now legitimately mutates derivation state (requeue rows) on a thread with transient failures; view-compact.test.ts's record-untouched assertions remain valid only because the file's first default compact performs the one requeue — noted in the amended test comment.\",\"The runtime issue that forced this primitive-path recovery is recorded as lessons entry 6 in the team-impl-log: composed story-lead runs cannot recover from transient provider failures (resume returns the blocked package without redispatching, and the 51-turn partial session left no continuation handle).\"]},\"openQuestions\":[],\"specDeviations\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Run the story-verify follow-up on the retained verifier handle (codex/019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6) against SV-03-001/SV-03-002 closure, then self-review sign-off and the story receipt/commit. CLI parity leg for sweep (TC-3.3 execution half) lands in Story 5's process suite as planned.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/009-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:02:56.450Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T17:19:14.131Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
